---
import AvalonIUDemoPlayer from "../components/AvalonIUDemo.svelte";

const manifestUrl =
  "https://media.dlib.indiana.edu/media_objects/3r074z37q/manifest.json";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Avalon Interop Demo - IIIF Transcript Player</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content='A production Avalon manifest from Indiana University&apos;s Media Collections Online, read step by step: Choice-wrapped HLS renditions, a supplementing WebVTT annotation, and annotations="auto" turning it into an interactive transcript.'
    />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Crimson+Pro:wght@400;600;700;900&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
  </head>
  <body class="font-sans bg-parchment-100 bg-linen text-ink-900 antialiased">
    <!-- Navigation -->
    <nav
      class="fixed top-0 left-0 right-0 z-50 bg-parchment-50/95 backdrop-blur-sm border-b-2 border-ink-200"
    >
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between h-16">
          <div class="flex items-center">
            <a
              href="."
              class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-ink-900 tracking-tight"
            >
              IIIF Transcript Player
            </a>
          </div>
          <div class="hidden md:flex items-center space-x-8">
            <a
              href="."
              class="text-ink-600 hover:text-terracotta-500 transition-colors font-medium"
              >Home</a
            >
            <a
              href="https://github.com/umd-mith/svelte-iiif-transcript-player"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
              class="text-ink-600 hover:text-terracotta-500 transition-colors font-medium"
            >
              GitHub
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="pt-32 pb-16 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 border-b-2 border-ink-200">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="text-sm font-mono text-terracotta-400 mb-6 tracking-wider">
          DEMO
        </div>
        <h1
          class="text-5xl md:text-6xl font-serif font-bold text-ink-900 mb-6 leading-tight"
        >
          Reading an Avalon Manifest
        </h1>
        <p
          class="text-xl text-ink-600 mb-4 max-w-3xl font-serif leading-relaxed"
        >
          <a
            href="https://avalonmediasystem.org/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="text-terracotta-500 hover:text-terracotta-600 underline"
            >Avalon Media System</a
          > is the audiovisual repository software many university libraries run.
          Every public Avalon item publishes a IIIF Presentation 3 manifest, and this
          library plays them without Avalon-specific code. This page walks through
          one for real — a production item from Indiana University's <a
            href="https://media.dlib.indiana.edu/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="text-terracotta-500 hover:text-terracotta-600 underline"
            >Media Collections Online</a
          > — and shows what the player does with each piece.
        </p>
        <p
          class="text-base text-ink-500 mb-8 max-w-3xl font-serif leading-relaxed"
        >
          The recording itself is a nice piece of circularity: Chris Colvard,
          Avalon's community technical lead, giving a 2017 talk titled <em
            >Beyond Images: Avalon and IIIF-AV</em
          > — a talk about the very interoperability that lets this player render
          it.
        </p>

        <!-- Step 1 -->
        <div class="bg-parchment-200 border-2 border-ink-200 p-6 mb-8">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-serif font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">
            1 — The media is a <code
              class="font-mono text-base bg-parchment-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
              >Choice</code
            > of HLS renditions
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-600 mb-4 font-serif leading-relaxed">
            On the canvas, the painting annotation's body is not a single video
            file. It is a <code
              class="font-mono text-xs bg-parchment-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
              >Choice</code
            > — Presentation 3's "here are alternatives, pick one" construct — holding
            Avalon's quality ladder as four HLS streams (<code
              class="font-mono text-xs bg-parchment-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
              >auto</code
            >, <code
              class="font-mono text-xs bg-parchment-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
              >high</code
            >, <code
              class="font-mono text-xs bg-parchment-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
              >medium</code
            >, <code
              class="font-mono text-xs bg-parchment-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
              >low</code
            >):
          </p>
          <pre
            class="text-xs font-mono overflow-x-auto text-ink-800 mb-4"><code>{`"body": {
  "type": "Choice",
  "choiceHint": "user",
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "https://media.dlib.indiana.edu/master_files/ft848t943/auto.m3u8",
      "type": "Video",
      "format": "application/x-mpegURL",
      "height": 1080, "width": 1920, "duration": 3217.04,
      "label": { "none": ["auto"] }
    },
    { "...": "high.m3u8, medium.m3u8, low.m3u8 follow the same shape" }
  ]
}`}</code></pre>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-600 font-serif leading-relaxed">
            The player's manifest parsing resolves a <code
              class="font-mono text-xs bg-parchment-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
              >Choice</code
            > to its first <code
              class="font-mono text-xs bg-parchment-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
              >Sound</code
            >/<code
              class="font-mono text-xs bg-parchment-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
              >Video</code
            > member — here the <code
              class="font-mono text-xs bg-parchment-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
              >auto</code
            > stream, which is itself adaptive. The <code
              class="font-mono text-xs bg-parchment-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
              >application/x-mpegURL</code
            > format marks it as HLS, so the player attaches <code
              class="font-mono text-xs bg-parchment-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
              >hls.js</code
            > (Safari plays HLS natively). Playback runs off IU's streaming server,
            end to end.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 2 -->
        <div class="bg-parchment-200 border-2 border-ink-200 p-6 mb-8">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-serif font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">
            2 — The transcript is a <code
              class="font-mono text-base bg-parchment-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
              >supplementing</code
            > WebVTT annotation
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-600 mb-4 font-serif leading-relaxed">
            Alongside the painting annotation, the canvas carries a second
            annotation page. Its one annotation has motivation <code
              class="font-mono text-xs bg-parchment-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
              >supplementing</code
            > — Presentation 3's word for content that accompanies the media rather
            than being the media — and its body is the WebVTT caption file Avalon
            already maintains for this item:
          </p>
          <pre
            class="text-xs font-mono overflow-x-auto text-ink-800 mb-4"><code>{`{
  "type": "Annotation",
  "motivation": "supplementing",
  "body": {
    "id": "https://media.dlib.indiana.edu/master_files/ft848t943/supplemental_files/2925/captions",
    "type": "Text",
    "format": "text/vtt",
    "language": "eng"
  },
  "target": "https://media.dlib.indiana.edu/media_objects/3r074z37q/manifest/canvas/ft848t943"
}`}</code></pre>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-600 font-serif leading-relaxed">
            Nothing here was made for this player. Avalon generates this shape
            for every item that has captions; the annotation simply points at
            the same <code
              class="font-mono text-xs bg-parchment-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
              >text/vtt</code
            > file the repository serves its own player.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 3 -->
        <div class="bg-parchment-200 border-2 border-ink-200 p-6 mb-8">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-serif font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">
            3 — <code
              class="font-mono text-base bg-parchment-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
              >annotations="auto"</code
            > joins the two
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-600 mb-4 font-serif leading-relaxed">
            The host passes one prop and writes no VTT-parsing code:
          </p>
          <pre
            class="text-sm font-mono overflow-x-auto text-ink-800 mb-4"><code>{`<IIIFPlayer.Root manifestUrl="https://media.dlib.indiana.edu/media_objects/3r074z37q/manifest.json"
                 annotations="auto">
  ...
</IIIFPlayer.Root>`}</code></pre>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-600 font-serif leading-relaxed">
            <code
              class="font-mono text-xs bg-parchment-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
              >"auto"</code
            > looks first for annotations embedded in the manifest itself (<code
              class="font-mono text-xs bg-parchment-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
              >TextualBody</code
            >, the <a
              href="/svelte-iiif-transcript-player/htmlannotations-demo"
              class="text-terracotta-500 hover:text-terracotta-600 underline"
              >AVAnnotate shape</a
            >). This manifest has none, so it fetches the <code
              class="font-mono text-xs bg-parchment-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
              >supplementing</code
            > WebVTT, reduces each cue to plain text, and builds the interactive transcript
            from it — for this talk, nearly nine hundred segments, each one a click-to-seek
            target and searchable below. Because the transcript panel now shows the
            caption text, the player hides the native caption track once per canvas
            so the words aren't displayed twice; the same file still drives closed
            captions if a viewer turns them back on.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div
          class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-6 text-sm text-ink-500 border-t border-l-4 border-terracotta-300 pt-6 pl-6"
        >
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <div class="w-2 h-2 bg-terracotta-400 rotate-45"></div>
            <span class="font-medium">No Avalon-specific code</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <div class="w-2 h-2 bg-terracotta-400 rotate-45"></div>
            <span class="font-medium">Choice-wrapped HLS resolved</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <div class="w-2 h-2 bg-terracotta-400 rotate-45"></div>
            <span class="font-medium"
              >Transcript from the repository's own VTT</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Live Demo -->
    <section
      class="py-16 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 bg-parchment-50 border-b-2 border-ink-200"
    >
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto">
        <div class="mb-8">
          <h2
            class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-serif font-bold text-ink-900 mb-4"
          >
            Beyond Images: Avalon and IIIF-AV (2017)
          </h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-ink-600 max-w-3xl font-serif leading-relaxed">
            Streamed live from Indiana University — the video from IU's Wowza
            streaming server via HLS, the transcript from IU's caption file,
            both located through nothing but the manifest.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white border-2 border-ink-200 shadow-2xl p-6 md:p-10">
          <AvalonIUDemoPlayer client:load {manifestUrl} />
        </div>

        <div class="mt-6 text-sm text-ink-500">
          <p>
            Source manifest:
            <a
              href={manifestUrl}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
              class="text-terracotta-500 hover:text-terracotta-600 underline break-all"
            >
              {manifestUrl}
            </a>
            · <a
              href="https://media.dlib.indiana.edu/media_objects/3r074z37q"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
              class="text-terracotta-500 hover:text-terracotta-600 underline"
              >item page on Media Collections Online</a
            >
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            This item is public and its manifest carries no IIIF Auth services.
            An access-restricted Avalon item would parse the same way but fail
            at the media request; the player reports that failure with error
            source <code
              class="font-mono text-xs bg-parchment-200 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
              >"auth"</code
            > so a host page can send the viewer to the repository's own login. This
            page depends on IU's servers — if the demo is down, the manifest link
            above will say so quickly.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <footer class="py-12 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 bg-ink-900 text-ink-400">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto text-center">
        <p class="mb-4">
          Built by <a
            href="https://mith.umd.edu"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="text-terracotta-400 hover:text-terracotta-300"
            >Maryland Institute for Technology in the Humanities</a
          >
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm">
          Licensed under BSD-3-Clause-Clear • <a
            href="https://github.com/umd-mith/svelte-iiif-transcript-player"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="text-terracotta-400 hover:text-terracotta-300"
            >View on GitHub</a
          >
        </p>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
